    <string name="msp_settings_about_link_failed">Could not open a browser: %1$s</string>

    <!--
      Body of the \"what's new\" dialog. **Update this on every release, in all three
      language files.** `\n` is a line break; lines starting with a bullet are laid out as items.
    -->
    <string name="msp_settings_about_whats_new_body">This release focuses on reordering lists and fixing the playback controls.\n\n· Playlists: both the playlist list and a playlist\'s items can be reordered by long-pressing a whole row, and the order is saved; a new playlist goes to the end\n· Library: with several items selected, \"add to playlist\" and \"play\" follow the order you tapped them in, so tapping in reverse no longer yields a reversed queue\n· Player: fixed the transport row overflowing on 360dp-wide screens (the last button was squeezed into a sliver); it is now laid out from the width actually available\n· Network: cleartext HTTP is allowed, so http:// addresses such as a NAS on your LAN or a local LLM server now work\n· Already there: playback with an FFmpeg software-decoding fallback, sidecar matching and line-by-line translation, offline subtitle generation, themes, library and playlists\n\nKnown limits: a mismatched model language is only reported, never switched automatically; no 32-bit native libraries.</string>

